0-Q/A","filedAt":"2026-05-18","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0001956741","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1956741/000121390026058489/ea0291213-10qa1_cleancore.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/ca2cab073bd14b4e10967badbc413d748c522694a917418cbca4e2bdad98fdc6.bin","sha256":"ca2cab073bd14b4e10967badbc413d748c522694a917418cbca4e2bdad98fdc6"}},{"id":"64e11dfb5022ff107987f3275a8dc70007fc677fcf8fe4d912276b2cb4fd5564","quote":"The following presents a reconciliation of the impacted financial statement line items as filed to the restated amounts as of March 31, 2026. The previously reported amounts reflect those included in the Original Filing on Form 10-Q for the three months ended March 31, 2026, filed with the SEC on May 11, 2026. These amounts are labeled as “As Filed” in the tables below. The amounts labeled “Restatement Adjustments” represent the effects of this restatement due to the reduction in assets on the balance sheet and increase in general and administrative expenses. As a result, change in fair value of digital assets and net income are also impacted.","context":"A previously disclosed Board of Directors resolution dated February 27, 2026, in connection with the cancellation of an asset management agreement, resulted in the non-cash transfer of 70,000,000 Dogecoins. This transaction was not recorded in the Company’s accounting system, nor verified against an independent source during reconciling. As a result, the Company’s digital assets were overstated, while general and administrative expenses were understated.","section":"ITEM 1. FINANCIAL STATEMENTS.","block":79,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-058489","form":"10-Q/A","filedAt":"2026-05-18","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0001956741","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1956741/000121390026058489/ea0291213-10qa1_cleancore.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/ca2cab073bd14b4e10967badbc413d748c522694a917418cbca4e2bdad98fdc6.bin","sha256":"ca2cab073bd14b4e10967badbc413d748c522694a917418cbca4e2bdad98fdc6"}},{"id":"c62273109a128a2b631bf9334e9d9504acd83b285d0fb97ea30b73c7655d1455","quote":"CC Acquisition Corp. was incorporated in the State of Nevada on August 23, 2022 for the sole purpose of acquiring substantially all of the assets of CleanCore Solutions, LLC, TetraClean Systems, LLC, and Food Safety Technologies, LLC, pursuant to an asset purchase agreement entered into by CC Acquisition Corp. with these three entities and their owners on October 17, 2022. On November 21, 2022, CC Acquisition Corp. changed its name to CleanCore Solutions, Inc. (“CleanCore US”). Since CleanCore US acquired substantially all of the assets of each of CleanCore Solutions, LLC, TetraClean Systems, LLC, and Food Safety Technologies, LLC, the business of these three entities is now operated by CleanCore US.","context":"1a. Organization and Business","section":"●Item 2, Management’s Discussion and Analysis","block":92,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-058489","form":"10-Q/A","filedAt":"2026-05-18","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0001956741","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1956741/000121390026058489/ea0291213-10qa1_cleancore.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/ca2cab073bd14b4e10967badbc413d748c522694a917418cbca4e2bdad98fdc6.bin","sha256":"ca2cab073bd14b4e10967badbc413d748c522694a917418cbca4e2bdad98fdc6"}},{"id":"c1194268e913cddf734846421ed60d2e34685c6bbc51cfa418a6557a81047216","quote":"On January 29, 2025, CleanCore established CleanCore Global Limited (“CleanCore Global,” and together with CleanCore US, the “Company”) as a wholly owned subsidiary in Ireland.","context":"CC Acquisition Corp. was incorporated in the State of Nevada on August 23, 2022 for the sole purpose of acquiring substantially all of the assets of CleanCore Solutions, LLC, TetraClean Systems, LLC, and Food Safety Technologies, LLC, pursuant to an asset purchase agreement entered into by CC Acquisition Corp. with these three entities and their owners on October 17, 2022. On November 21, 2022, CC Acquisition Corp. changed its name to CleanCore Solutions, Inc. (“CleanCore US”). Since CleanCore US acquired substantially all of the assets of each of CleanCore Solutions, LLC, TetraClean Systems, LLC, and Food Safety Technologies, LLC, the business of these three entities is now operated by CleanCore US.","section":"●Item 2, Management’s Discussion and Analysis","block":93,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-058489","form":"10-Q/A","filedAt":"2026-05-18","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0001956741","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1956741/000121390026058489/ea0291213-10qa1_cleancore.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/ca2cab073bd14b4e10967badbc413d748c522694a917418cbca4e2bdad98fdc6.bin","sha256":"ca2cab073bd14b4e10967badbc413d748c522694a917418cbca4e2bdad98fdc6"}},{"id":"718809a73e8083d08aa51df220fe22c5828f7810f6ea31d3cfa66157f0b3c20c","quote":"The Company specializes in the development and production of cleaning products that produce pure aqueous ozone products for professional, industrial, or home use. The Company has a patented nanobubble technology using aqueous ozone that it believes is highly effective in cleaning, sanitizing, and deodorizing surfaces and high-touch areas.","context":"On January 29, 2025, CleanCore established CleanCore Global Limited (“CleanCore Global,” and together with CleanCore US, the “Company”) as a wholly owned subsidiary in Ireland.","section":"●Item 2, Management’s Discussion and Analysis","block":94,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-058489","form":"10-Q/A","filedAt":"2026-05-18","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0001956741","url":"https://www.se